 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Gating
+
+The evaluation harness supports optional metric thresholds to gate CI pipelines on evaluation results:
+- `frai eval --threshold <metric>=<min>` (can be repeated)
+- Valid metrics: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`
+- Minimum values must be between 0 and 1
+- A metric with no score fails its threshold
+- Exit 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 for malformed inputs
+- JSON reports gain a `passed` field and `thresholds` array; Markdown reports gain a "Thresholds" section
+- `generateReport(thresholds)` in the SDK accepts an optional `{ metric_id: 0.9 }` object
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
